    "conclusion": "within_approval",
    "reasons": [
      "The previous exact candidate is rejected because the required complete verification timed out. Preserve its exact rejection and native failed summaries; no failed check, candidate conclusion or absent native code subject is turned into approval.",
      "Profiled native baseline resolution repeatedly starts Git processes. Query current canonical trusted refs and object types once per invocation, preserving symbolic-default/remote-main/local-main priority and commit validation; no long-lived cache, working-copy policy authority or real ref write is introduced.",
      "A real-Git regression constrains the common lookup to one process and checks ref movement, non-symbolic remote HEAD, shadow tags, annotated commit peeling, invalid-type fallback and absent-base rejection. Existing assertions and verification selection/deadlines are unchanged.",
      "Final targeted checks pass 23 cases including approval and first-policy bootstrap plus the public integration scenario; retain source-specific latency boundaries and first A host test records. The final new subject still requires native complete verification and exact external approval."
    ],
